# Movie Finder — imdbapi-client Cursor Rules

This file is a legacy fallback. Cursor loads the richer MDC rules from `.cursor/rules/` automatically.

If your IDE supports MDC rules, the following files apply:
- `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` — always active (IMDb client context, adapter pattern)
- `.cursor/rules/python.mdc` — activates on `**/*.py`
- `.cursor/rules/architect.mdc` — activates when designing API contract changes
- `.cursor/rules/developer.mdc` — activates when implementing issues

---

## Quick reference

**Repo:** `aharbii/imdbapi-client` · Primary context: `CLAUDE.md`

**Non-negotiables:**
- Adapter pattern — client wraps imdbapi.dev and maps to internal domain types; callers never see raw HTTP
- `mypy --strict` must pass — no `type: ignore` without explanatory comment
- No bare `except:` — always catch specific types (httpx exceptions, pydantic ValidationError)
- Async all the way — all I/O uses `httpx.AsyncClient`
- Known issue #8: retry base delay 30s blocks SSE — do not increase it further
- `make check` (ruff + mypy + pytest) must pass before any PR
- Conventional Commits: `fix(imdbapi): summary`
- Disclose AI tool + model in every PR
